WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.941
A minimal setup that earns its keep.

2
00:00:02.221 --> 00:00:07.960
For most repositories, five pieces cover the checks and balances that matter: a short CLAUDE.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:26.203
md with the test command; a PostToolUse hook that runs fast checks (formatter, linter, quick tests) after edits; a Stop hook that runs the suite before Claude can finish; a deny rule plus a PreToolUse hook protecting the few paths that must never change without a person;

4
00:00:26.483 --> 00:00:28.531
and a read-only reviewer subagent.

5
00:00:28.811 --> 00:00:33.973
Add skills as procedures repeat and MCP servers as systems are needed.

6
00:00:34.253 --> 00:00:38.115
The lab’s setups/full/ is this setup for a tiny repo.

7
00:00:38.395 --> 00:00:43.856
Run it, read every file, and then measure whether it changes outcomes compared with a bare repo.

8
00:00:44.136 --> 00:00:48.595
That measurement, not the setup itself, is the point of the elective project.
